<div class="page public-page public-article">
    <header class="public-intro"><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>How the Class 9 MCQ Bank handles account, exam, visit, and advertising data.</p></header>
    <article class="card report-card public-copy">
        <h2>Account and practice data</h2>
        <p>Registration asks for your full name, email, mobile number, school name and password. The site stores a password hash. Signed-in practice saves your test selections, answers, scores and timing so you can continue tests and review progress. Administrators can view account and test information for support and reporting.</p>
        <p>The public sample quiz grades your answers for the current request. Its questions, results and answers are not written to your student exam history.</p>
        <h2>Browser storage and visit logs</h2>
        <p>The site uses browser session storage for the sign-in token and draft exam selections. Signing out clears the sign-in token. A first-party visit cookie groups activity by browser session. Visit logs can include the page path, time, event type, IP address, browser information and an account ID when the visitor is identified. The contact form also uses a security cookie to verify submissions.</p>
        <h2>Contact messages</h2>
        <p>The site stores your name, email address and message when you submit the contact form. This information lets the site operator review your inquiry and reply when needed. Use the contact form for questions about your data or to request a correction or deletion.</p>
        <h2>Google AdSense and advertising</h2>
        <p>When ads are enabled, Google and other third-party vendors may read or place cookies or use similar technologies, such as web beacons, IP addresses and other identifiers, to serve and measure advertising. Google’s advertising cookies, including cookies associated with DoubleClick, may allow Google and its partners to personalize ads based on prior visits to this site or other sites.</p>
        <p>You can opt out of Google’s personalized advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">Google Ads Settings</a>. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/contact">Contact us about privacy</a>
    </article>
</div>
